---
args: {"atlas": "IntegrationAtlas", "change": "CutoverChange"}
returns: "CutoverReview"
---
1. Compare change.expectedAtlasRevision and the actual sponsor authority with atlas. For stale, unsupported, missing-wave or already-executed changes, preserve the atlas and return CutoverReview { atlas, rescheduledKeys: [], preservedEffectiveKeys: exact effective decision/wave keys, unresolved: the precise changed source or missing authority }. Do not move an executed wave retroactively.
2. For the supported selected unexecuted waves, change plannedExecutionAt to change.requestedExecutionAt and attach the source-bound reason and sponsor evidence. Preserve effectiveDecisionAt, rollback boundary, actual integrity/acceptance receipts and every prior decision. Reassess time-sensitive prerequisites at the new date; retain stale authority or integrity checks as wave holds.
3. Bind nextAtlas as IntegrationAtlas { revision: advance only when a new supported scheduling change was made, senses: atlas.senses, bridges: atlas.bridges, handoffs: atlas.handoffs, scenarios: atlas.scenarios, waves: changed selected waves plus every unaffected wave, retainedOrganizationAliases: atlas.retainedOrganizationAliases, decisionHistory: atlas.decisionHistory plus the actual rescheduling decision and source references once }. Return { atlas: nextAtlas, rescheduledKeys: changed wave keys, preservedEffectiveKeys: historical effective decision keys, unresolved: remaining prerequisite and authority holds }. An identical approved reschedule is a no-op; a postponed cutover never rewrites historical effectiveness.
